{
  "slug": "corned-beef-and-turnip-hash",
  "title": "Corned Beef and Turnip Hash",
  "blurb": "A simple stovetop hash with tender corned beef, soft turnips and golden onions in a creamy sauce.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat the canola oil in a large frying pan over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the chopped onions and cook for 3 to 4 minutes until softened and starting to colour.",
    "Add the chopped corned beef and turnips to the pan, spreading them out evenly.",
    "Cook without stirring for 5 minutes to let the bottom crisp up, then stir and cook for another 5 minutes.",
    "Pour in the heavy cream and season with black pepper, stirring gently to coat everything.",
    "Simmer for 3 to 4 minutes until the cream has thickened slightly and the hash is heated through."
  ],
